# SEQ REC tapped twice (app/ui.c rec_twice): live recording, counted in. Stopped: the first tap's step record undone,
# a bar of count-in (COUNT-IN off), then the transport from step 1, recording; a key in the count-in's last half step
# lands on step 1. Playing: recording from the next bar line, the rest of the bar the count-in (less than a beat of it
# left: the bar after); a key half a sixteenth early lands on the bar's first step, one earlier is only heard; a REC
# press while it waits turns it off. The count-in clicks with the metronome off, and only the count-in does.
# (120 BPM: a sixteenth 125 ms, a bar 2000 ms; times from PLAY's press)
wait 300
plainproject
listen
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
# REC held + K1: the metronome off (it was "while recording")
press REC
turn K1 -2
release REC
wait 500
expect clicks 0
# stopped: tap, tap (the second's press: t 0 of the count-in)
tap REC
wait 60
expect steprec 1
tap REC
said COUNT-IN
wait 20
expect steprec 0
expect playing 1
expect rec 1
expect countin 1
wait 1850
expect countin 1
# t 1950, a key just before the count-in ends: step 1
key 0 down
wait 60
key 0 up
wait 40
expect countin 0
# t 2494: step 5
wait 440
key 2 down
wait 60
key 2 up
wait 1000
# the count-in's four beats and the bar's first, nothing after (the metronome off)
expect clicks 5
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
expect note 2 1 1 53
expect note 2 1 5 55
# playing, on T3 (an empty pattern): tap, tap at the bar's sixth sixteenth (t 720): recording from the next bar line
# (t 2000)
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 3
tap PLAY
wait 500
tap REC
wait 60
tap REC
said RECORDING
expect recatbar 1
expect rec 0
# while it waits: heard, not recorded (t 800)
key 5 down
wait 60
key 5 up
wait 1038
# t 1900, 100 ms before the line: heard only
key 7 down
wait 30
key 7 up
expect rec 0
wait 28
# t 1965, 35 ms before the line: it starts the recording, on step 1
key 4 down
wait 10
expect rec 1
expect recatbar 0
wait 20
key 4 up
wait 500
# t 2490: step 5
key 9 down
wait 60
key 9 up
wait 200
# the count-in's beats left (t 1000, 1500) and the line's (t 2000)
expect clicks 3
tap PLAY
expect note 3 1 1 57
expect note 3 1 5 62
expect note 3 1 7 0
expect note 3 1 16 0
# less than a beat left (tapped at sixteenth 13): the bar after; a REC press while it waits: off
tap PLAY
wait 1500
tap REC
wait 60
tap REC
expect recatbar 2
wait 500
expect recatbar 1
expect rec 0
tap REC
said RECORD OFF
expect recatbar 0
# (the first line's click, t 2000: the count-in had a bar to go)
expect clicks 1
wait 2200
expect rec 0
expect clicks 0
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
# the metronome while recording again: a double tap's count-in clicks as before, and so does the recording
press REC
turn K1 1
release REC
wait 300
expect clicks 0
tap REC
wait 60
tap REC
wait 3860
expect clicks 8
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
